# Coding style

- TypeScript strict. Avoid `any` without justification.
- `verbatimModuleSyntax`: use `import type` for types.
- Validate every trust boundary with Zod (`@mysimcha/shared` or colocated schemas).
- Named exports for shared helpers. No silent catch blocks.
- Workspace deps use `"@mysimcha/foo": "workspace:*"`.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
try {
  await save(input);
} catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD
const data = schema.parse(input);
try {
  await save(data);
} catch (error) {
  throw error;
}
```
